{
  "claims": [
    {
      "component_id": "C1",
      "text": "In a cross-sectional study of 48 Behçet's disease (BD) patients and 35 healthy controls who all underwent transthoracic echocardiography, the BD group showed significantly lower absolute GLS (18.51 ± 2.02 vs. 19.53 ± 1.71, p = 0.018), lower absolute right ventricular free wall strain (RVFWS; 25.35 ± 3.32 vs. 26.87 ± 3.01, p = 0.047), and lower coronary sinus flow (CSF) index (2.62 ± 0.99 vs. 3.58 ± 1.17 mL/min/g, p < 0.001) compared with the control group.",
      "cite": ["PMID:42054004"],
      "evidence_ids": ["E4", "E7"]
    },
    {
      "component_id": "C2",
      "text": "The combined model using GLS and the CSF index exhibited a higher diagnostic performance in distinguishing BD patients compared to their individual use, with an AUC of 0.759, 80.9% sensitivity and 65.7% specificity.",
      "cite": ["PMID:42054004"],
      "evidence_ids": ["E11"]
    }
  ],
  "confidence": 0.95,
  "evidence_status": "complete",
  "evidence_gap": ""
}

{
  "claims": [
    {
      "component_id": "C1",
      "text": "In a retrospective study of 1531 patients with STEMI who underwent cardiac MRI, HF-related events were defined as unplanned hospitalization for HF and heart transplantation; over a median follow-up of 50.9 months, 262 patients reached the composite endpoints, of whom 104 developed HF-related events. In the adjusted analysis, diabetes, Killip class >= 2, microvascular obstruction, intramyocardial hemorrhage, ventricular aneurysm, infarct size, LA reservoir strain (hazard ratio 0.93 [95% CI, 0.91-0.96]; P < 0.001) and conduit strain (hazard ratio 0.94 [95% CI, 0.89-0.99]; P = 0.02) were associated with HF-related events. The HF risk remained low in patients with relatively preserved LA reservoir function (>= 23%), regardless of ejection fraction performance at discharge, whereas among populations with normal LVEF and with reduced LVEF, patients with LA reservoir strain < 23% had a 2- to 5-fold increased risk of experiencing HF-related events. Reduced LA reservoir strain was therefore independently associated with HF-related events in patients with STEMI, which can improve risk stratification across different LVEF levels and potentially guide decision-making for clinical therapy.",
      "cite": ["PMID:41894993"],
      "evidence_ids": ["E6", "E8", "E9", "E10", "E11", "E12", "E13"]
    },
    {
      "component_id": "C2",
      "text": "In a retrospective analysis of 1147 patients with chronic heart failure and LVEF < 50% who underwent comprehensive transthoracic echocardiography between January 2018 and May 2023, LASr and RASr were assessed by two-dimensional speckle-tracking echocardiography and patients were stratified into four groups according to high or low LASr and RASr based on median values. The primary endpoint was a composite of cardiac death or HF hospitalization, and during a median follow-up of 34 months, 221 composite events occurred. Event-free survival differed significantly among the four groups (log-rank test, P < 0.01), and patients with concomitantly low LASr and low RASr had the highest risk of cardiac death or HF hospitalization. After adjustment for age, sex, LVEF, left atrial volume index and tricuspid regurgitation velocity, combined low LASr and low RASr remained independently associated with adverse outcomes (hazard ratio 2.43, 95% confidence interval 1.64-3.61; P < 0.01), such that combined assessment of LASr and RASr identified a distinct high-risk phenotype in patients with chronic heart failure and reduced LVEF.",
      "cite": ["PMID:41932653"],
      "evidence_ids": ["E17", "E19", "E20", "E22", "E23", "E24", "E25", "E26"]
    }
  ],
  "confidence": 0.9,
  "evidence_status": "complete",
  "evidence_gap": ""
}

{
  "claims": [
    {
      "component_id": "C1",
      "text": "In the study by PMID:41698552, a total of 78 women with LVOTO (109 pregnancies) were included, and gestational increases in LVOT gradients were transient, regressing to baseline levels postpartum for most; the authors concluded that pregnancy causes an increase in LVOT gradients but no significant disease progression warranting either antenatal or postpartum intervention, except in patients who had severe LVOTO preconception.",
      "cite": ["PMID:41698552"],
      "evidence_ids": ["E9", "E10", "E14"]
    },
    {
      "component_id": "C2",
      "text": "The primary endpoint was the need for postpartum intervention, while the secondary endpoints were a composite of adverse clinical outcomes and postpartum intervention; postpartum intervention was required in 11% of pregnancies within a median of 6.3 (4.4-9.2) years.",
      "cite": ["PMID:41698552"],
      "evidence_ids": ["E8", "E11"]
    },
    {
      "component_id": "C2",
      "text": "Predictors of the primary endpoint (need for postpartum intervention) were baseline LVOTO severity (HR = 29.6, p < 0.01), antenatal LVOTO severity (HR = 21.1, p < 0.01), and postpartum LVOTO severity (HR = 18.3, p < 0.01); patients with inherently severe LVOTO at baseline (n = 8, 10%) had a significantly increased risk of postpartum intervention, whereas those with transiently severe LVOTO during pregnancy did not.",
      "cite": ["PMID:41698552"],
      "evidence_ids": ["E12", "E13"]
    },
    {
      "component_id": "C3",
      "text": "PMID:41698552 was a retrospective, observational study conducted between 2009 and 2023 in two tertiary centres; because this design is observational rather than randomised, it cannot establish that any treatment or intervention caused the observed clinical outcomes, and its reported associations between LVOTO severity and postpartum intervention cannot be interpreted as treatment effects.",
      "cite": ["PMID:41698552"],
      "evidence_ids": ["E5"]
    }
  ],
  "confidence": 0.9,
  "evidence_status": "complete",
  "evidence_gap": ""
}

{
  "claims": [
    {
      "component_id": "C1",
      "text": "The supplied atrial-strain evidence comes from a single retrospective analysis of 1147 patients with chronic heart failure and left ventricular ejection fraction <50% who underwent comprehensive transthoracic echocardiography between January 2018 and May 2023, in which left atrial reservoir strain (LASr) and right atrial reservoir strain (RASr) were assessed using two-dimensional speckle-tracking echocardiography and patients were stratified into four groups by high or low LASr and RASr based on median values.",
      "cite": ["PMID:41932653"],
      "evidence_ids": ["E4", "E5", "E6"]
    },
    {
      "component_id": "C1",
      "text": "That study's primary endpoint was a composite of cardiac death or HF hospitalization, and it reported a prognostic association rather than a management comparison: after adjustment for age, sex, LVEF, left atrial volume index and tricuspid regurgitation velocity, combined low LASr and low RASr remained independently associated with adverse outcomes (hazard ratio 2.43, 95% confidence interval 1.64-3.61; P < 0.01).",
      "cite": ["PMID:41932653"],
      "evidence_ids": ["E7", "E11", "E12"]
    },
    {
      "component_id": "C1",
      "text": "Because the design retrospectively observed patients who received comprehensive transthoracic echocardiography without assigning or comparing an atrial-strain-guided management strategy against standard management, it can support inference about the prognostic value of bi-atrial reservoir strain but cannot establish that atrial-strain-guided management improves heart-failure outcomes.",
      "cite": ["PMID:41932653"],
      "evidence_ids": ["E4", "E13", "E14"]
    }
  ],
  "confidence": 0.85,
  "evidence_status": "partial",
  "evidence_gap": "The retrieved evidence does not establish improvement in heart-failure outcomes with atrial-strain-guided management versus standard management; no atrial-strain-guided management arm or standard-management comparator was reported."
}

{
